  },
  {
    "id": "isopure-clear-protein-powder-review-myprotein-clear-whey",
    "name": "Myprotein Clear Whey Isolate, 35 Servings (1.9 lb)",
    "brand": "Myprotein",
    "badge": "Cheaper Alternative",
    "category": "Clear whey isolate",
    "description": "Myprotein's clear whey is the obvious budget rival. Its US label lists 20 g of protein in a 25 g scoop for about 80 calories in Lemonade, per Myprotein's site when we last checked, and Myprotein says the product is Informed Choice certified. The Lemonade label we read used sucralose and acesulfame potassium, although the current Amazon listing calls it naturally flavored, so check the sweetener line on the tub you get. At the Amazon price we saw ($36.66), it is about $1.31 per 25 g.",
    "pros": [
      "About $1.31 per 25 g, far below Isopure Clear",
      "Informed Choice certified, per Myprotein",
      "Wide flavor range"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Lemonade label we read used sucralose and acesulfame potassium",
      "Some flavors use artificial colors, per Myprotein's labels",
      "Protein listed as hydrolyzed whey on the US label"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The pick if you want a clear whey with a certification and a lower price, and do not mind artificial sweeteners.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein / serving": "20 g per 25 g scoop (label)",
