        <div id="buyer-feedback" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            8. What Do Buyers Say About Isopure Clear Taste and Mixing?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Buyers mostly describe Isopure Clear as light and refreshing, closer to a lightly sweetened sports drink or flavored water than a protein shake. We have not tasted it ourselves, so everything in this section is a summary of buyer reviews and the brand's own directions, not our testing.
          </p>

          <p>
            Foam is the most common complaint. Clear whey isolates foam when shaken, and Isopure tells you to shake, not stir, one scoop in 14 to 18 fl oz of cold water and then wait about a minute for the foam to settle. Buyers who skip that wait tend to report a frothy first few sips. Isopure says the newer formula has less foam, so recent reviews may read better than older ones.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Which Isopure Clear flavor do buyers like best?</h3>

          <p>
            Citrus Lemonade and Tropical Punch are the flavors buyers mention most often, and they are also the ones Isopure keeps in the largest tub, which suggests they sell best. Pineapple Orange Banana has a loyal following. The tea flavors are newer, so there is less feedback on them, and anyone avoiding caffeine should skip them anyway.
          </p>

          <p>
            Other recurring comments: some buyers say a faint protein or milky aftertaste still comes through, especially in warmer water, and a few find the stevia sweetness noticeable. Mixing it colder and with a little more water helps on both counts. Buyers who use it in place of juice or soda tend to be happier than buyers who expected it to replace a creamy chocolate shake.
          </p>

          <p>
            A tip from the brand itself is to mix two flavors together or freeze the drink into ice pops. For more ideas on getting clear whey to taste good, our <a href="/best-clear-protein-powder/">clear protein guide</a> covers mixing temperature and water ratios.
          </p>
        </div>

