                  It contains dairy, because whey isolate comes from milk, and Isopure's own FAQ says it is not dairy-free. Lactose is a different matter: isolate is filtered to remove most of it, and Isopure's Amazon listing calls the powder lactose free. Many lactose-sensitive people tolerate it, but anyone with a milk allergy should avoid it completely.
                </p>
